    "id": "train-7202",
    "question": "Chris has twelve marbles, and Ryan has twenty-eight marbles. If they put marbles together in a pile and then each takes away 1/4 of marbles from the pile, calculate the number of marbles remaining in the pile.",
    "gold": "20",
    "answer": "If Chris and Ryan put together their marbles in a pile, the pile will have 12+28 = <<12+28=40>>40 marbles.\nIf they then take 1/4 of the marbles each, every person will receive 1/4*40 = <<1/4*40=10>>10 marbles.\nBoth of them will have taken a total of 10+10 = <<10+10=20>>20 marbles.\nThe number of marbles remaining in the pile is 40-20 = <<40-20=20>>20\n#### 20"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To solve the problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the total number of marbles in the pile.\n2. Calculate how many marbles each person takes away from the pile.\n3. Subtract the number of marbles taken away from the total number of marbles in the pile.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total number of marbles in the pile.\nChris has 12 marbles and Ryan has 28 marbles. So, the total number of marbles is:\n\\[ 12 + 28 = 40 \\]\n\nStep 2: Calculate how many marbles each person takes away from the pile.\nEach person takes away \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) of the total number of marbles. So, each person takes away:\n\\[ \\frac{1}{4} \\times 40 = 10 \\]\nSince there are two people, the total number of marbles taken away is:\n\\[ 10 + 10 = 20 \\]\n\nStep 3: Subtract the number of marbles taken away from the total number of marbles in the pile.\nThe number of marbles remaining in the pile is:\n\\[ 40 - 20 = 20 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of marbles remaining in the pile is \\(\\boxed{20}\\).",
